{"name":"Brandy Snaps","hex":"#b58e8b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brandy snaps","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of brandy snap"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brandy_snaps"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brandy snaps","blocks":[{"text":"Brandy snaps are a popular snack or dessert food in the United Kingdom, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, similar to the Italian cannoli. They are often tubular, brittle, sweet, baked casings that are typically 10 centimetres (4 in) long and 2 centimetres (1 in) in diameter. Brandy snaps are customarily served filled with whipped cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Brandy_snap.jpg/330px-Brandy_snap.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brandy_snaps","wikidata":"Q4957262"},{"title":"Brandy","blocks":[{"text":"Brandy is a liquor produced by distilling wine. Brandy generally contains 35–60% alcohol by volume and is typically consumed as an after-dinner digestif. Some brandies are aged in wooden casks. Others are coloured with caramel colouring to imitate the effect of ageing, and some are produced using a combination of ageing and colouring. Varieties of wine brandy can be found across the winemaking world. Among the most renowned are Cognac and Armagnac from southwestern France."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Cognac_glass.jpg/330px-Cognac_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brandy","wikidata":"Q146470"},{"title":"Snaps","blocks":[{"text":"In the Nordic countries, especially Denmark and Sweden, but not in Iceland, snaps, among many nicknames, is a small shot of a strong alcoholic beverage taken during the course of a meal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Snaps_at_a_sittning_%28brightened%29.jpg/330px-Snaps_at_a_sittning_%28brightened%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snaps","wikidata":"Q4166575"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Bodega-TioPepe-Jerez-Dsc02980.jpg/500px-Bodega-TioPepe-Jerez-Dsc02980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Bodega-TioPepe-Jerez-Dsc02980.jpg/1280px-Bodega-TioPepe-Jerez-Dsc02980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Bodega-TioPepe-Jerez-Dsc02980.jpg/500px-Bodega-TioPepe-Jerez-Dsc02980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brandy de Jerez in barrels aging","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABodega-TioPepe-Jerez-Dsc02980.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Fem_m%C3%A4n_h%C3%B6jer_sina_snapsglas_ute_i_en_tr%C3%A4dg%C3%A5rd_st%C3%A5ende_vid_ett_tr%C3%A4dg%C3%A5rdsbord_med_kaffekoppar_och_flaskor_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0048890.jpg/500px-Fem_m%C3%A4n_h%C3%B6jer_sina_snapsglas_ute_i_en_tr%C3%A4dg%C3%A5rd_st%C3%A5ende_vid_ett_tr%C3%A4dg%C3%A5rdsbord_med_kaffekoppar_och_flaskor_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0048890.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Fem_m%C3%A4n_h%C3%B6jer_sina_snapsglas_ute_i_en_tr%C3%A4dg%C3%A5rd_st%C3%A5ende_vid_ett_tr%C3%A4dg%C3%A5rdsbord_med_kaffekoppar_och_flaskor_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0048890.jpg/500px-Fem_m%C3%A4n_h%C3%B6jer_sina_snapsglas_ute_i_en_tr%C3%A4dg%C3%A5rd_st%C3%A5ende_vid_ett_tr%C3%A4dg%C3%A5rdsbord_med_kaffekoppar_och_flaskor_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0048890.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Snaps drinking in Sweden, early 20th century.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFem_m%C3%A4n_h%C3%B6jer_sina_snapsglas_ute_i_en_tr%C3%A4dg%C3%A5rd_st%C3%A5ende_vid_ett_tr%C3%A4dg%C3%A5rdsbord_med_kaffekoppar_och_flaskor_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0048890.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Kr%C3%A4ftor_kr%C3%A4va_dessa_drycker.jpg/500px-Kr%C3%A4ftor_kr%C3%A4va_dessa_drycker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Kr%C3%A4ftor_kr%C3%A4va_dessa_drycker.jpg/1280px-Kr%C3%A4ftor_kr%C3%A4va_dessa_drycker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Kr%C3%A4ftor_kr%C3%A4va_dessa_drycker.jpg/500px-Kr%C3%A4ftor_kr%C3%A4va_dessa_drycker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Poster used at the 1922 Swedish prohibition referendum,  depicting a bottle of liquor and a glass for snaps together with cooked crayfish. The poster emphasizes that crayfish parties require snaps, and thus banning snaps would kill off crayfish parties with it. English: \"No! Crawfishes demand these beverages! You have to forgo crawfishes unless you vote NO on 27 August\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKr%C3%A4ftor_kr%C3%A4va_dessa_drycker.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Fishing Boats on the Beach by Anton Mauve Rijksdienst voor het Cultureel Erfgoed B918","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Fishing_Boats_on_the_Beach_by_Anton_Mauve_Rijksdienst_voor_het_Cultureel_Erfgoed_B918.jpg/500px-Fishing_Boats_on_the_Beach_by_Anton_Mauve_Rijksdienst_voor_het_Cultureel_Erfgoed_B918.jpg","ratio":1.424962852897474,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fishing_Boats_on_the_Beach_by_Anton_Mauve_Rijksdienst_voor_het_Cultureel_Erfgoed_B918.jpg","share":0.245},{"title":"Mauve surprise and Rosebud (Fabergé eggs)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip